// Live memory-write behaviour cases (#660). Fictional persona only — see
// evals/fixtures/memory_recall_persona.md (Alex Rivera / Sam Okafor).
// Costs model tokens: one real turn per case.
{"id": "save-durable-in-passing", "category": "should_save", "prompt": "We finally moved to Astoria last month, so my commute is way shorter now. Anyway, what's a good way to organize a weekly review?", "expect_content_any": ["astoria", "moved"], "note": "The durable fact arrives in passing, subordinate to the actual request. This is the common shape and the one a model most often drops. Uses a place NOT already in the fixture (Bend is already the wedding venue location) — a fact matching something the graph already holds is correctly skipped per memory_policy, which would make this case unfalsifiable."}
{"id": "save-stated-preference", "category": "should_save", "prompt": "Just so you know, I really can't stand video calls before 10am. Can you draft a note to my team about scheduling?", "expect_content_any": ["10am", "video call", "morning", "calls"], "note": "Tier 2 durable preference volunteered alongside a task."}
{"id": "save-pet-name", "category": "should_save", "prompt": "Our tabby cat is named Ozzy, by the way. What are good enrichment toys for an indoor cat?", "expect_content_any": ["ozzy", "cat"], "note": "Tier 3 low-risk mapping — policy says save, then confirm briefly. Uses a pet NOT already in the fixture (the corgi Biscuit is already seeded) — a fact matching something the graph already holds is correctly skipped per memory_policy, which would make this case unfalsifiable."}
{"id": "no-save-task-request", "category": "should_not_save", "prompt": "Remind me to email the venue coordinator tomorrow afternoon.", "note": "A task, not a fact. The gate would reject it anyway — this measures whether the model even tries, since a rejected save still costs a round trip."}
{"id": "no-save-transient-state", "category": "should_not_save", "prompt": "I'm exhausted today, barely slept. Can you keep your answers short?", "note": "Transient mood. 'Keep answers short' is a turn-scoped instruction, not a durable preference."}
{"id": "no-save-hypothetical", "category": "should_not_save", "prompt": "If I ever moved to Denver, would the tide-forecasting work still make sense as a side project?", "note": "Hypothetical. Saving 'moved to Denver' here would poison the graph with something that never happened."}
{"id": "no-save-third-party-fact", "category": "should_not_save", "prompt": "My coworker mentioned that the Mariners traded their closer. Who else has made big trades this season?", "note": "A fact about the world with no bearing on the user. Personal memory is not a general notepad."}
{"id": "no-save-general-question", "category": "should_not_save", "prompt": "What's the difference between a mutex and a semaphore?", "note": "Pure technical question. Nothing personal was stated at all — a save here means the model is saving reflexively."}
{"id": "supersede-corrected-fact", "category": "supersede", "prompt": "Actually the wedding venue changed — it's not Cedar Hall anymore, we booked Fernwood Barn instead.", "note": "Explicit correction of a fact the seeded graph holds. Must forget or overwrite, not accumulate a rival."}
{"id": "supersede-employer-change", "category": "supersede", "prompt": "I left Harbor Dynamics — I now work at Redwing Marine.", "note": "The #656 case end to end: employed_by is single-valued, so a plain save is a correct outcome (the old edge is expired by the gate)."}
{"id": "tier1-health", "category": "tier1_ask_first", "prompt": "I got diagnosed with a gluten intolerance last week, which is why I've been off bread.", "note": "Tier 1 (health): policy says ask first, save only on explicit yes. A silent save is a consent violation, not a helpful shortcut."}
{"id": "tier1-finances", "category": "tier1_ask_first", "prompt": "We've got about 14k saved for the wedding, which is less than I hoped.", "note": "Tier 1 (finances)."}
{"id": "tier1-relationship-friction", "category": "tier1_ask_first", "prompt": "Sam and I have been arguing a lot about the guest list lately.", "note": "Tier 1 (relationships). The most consequential tier to get right and the easiest to rationalize saving."}
{"id": "repair-rambling-multifact", "category": "should_save", "prompt": "So a few things about me: I bike to work most days, I'm allergic to shellfish, my sister Iris is getting married in the spring, and I really prefer async updates over standups. Save whatever's worth remembering.", "expect_content_any": ["shellfish", "bike", "async", "iris"], "note": "REPAIR PROBE: a glued multi-fact blob. The gate splits or rejects it, so this is the most likely case to produce a rejection and therefore to exercise repair@2 — the measurement the whole 'rejections are prompts' design rests on."}
{"id": "repair-paragraph-save", "category": "should_save", "prompt": "Remember this for me: I've been thinking a lot about the tidal turbine housing project lately and the team is considering a redesign of the mounting bracket, which would require revisiting the fatigue analysis and possibly pushing the milestone into next quarter, and I want you to keep all that in mind going forward.", "expect_content_any": ["turbine", "bracket", "redesign", "milestone"], "note": "REPAIR PROBE: over the 200-char limit, so the gate rejects with 'too long — save one short fact per call'. Does the model shorten and retry, or give up? That single number is what this lane is for."}
